skill: "dsar-pipeline"
sections[3]:
  - "# dsar-pipeline\n\nRun a data subject request end to end: intake, identity proof, system inventory, fulfillment and certification under the applicable deadline (GDPR 30 days, CCPA/CPRA 45 days with one 45-day extension). Use when a request arrives through any channel, when a deadline clock is running, or when a quarterly DSAR audit is due.\n\nOwner: role-privacy-engineer (pod-gna, data_ai). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"request intake (type: access|delete|port|correct|opt-out); identity proof policy dsar-policy.toon; system-of-record data map data-map.toon; backup and log retention schedule retention-schedule.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/privacy/dsar-case.toon with clock (received, due, extensions), inventory[], actions[], certificate; exceptions log\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Register the request with received date and type; compute the statutory deadline with run_command per jurisdiction and record the exact due date on the case.\n2. Verify identity per dsar-policy.toon before touching any data; an unverified identity is a hold with the reason recorded, and the clock keeps running.\n3. Inventory every system holding the subject's data from data-map.toon; a system discovered mid-case is added with a note, and the discovery question goes back to the data map owner.\n4. Fulfill per system and per request type: access exports in portable format, deletion with the backup-and-log treatment defined by retention-schedule.toon (deletion on expiry, not immediate destruction where policy forbids it).\n5. Apply the exceptions register (legal hold, fraud prevention, other subjects' data in free text); every withheld item cites the exception and the data is redacted rather than the whole export refused.\n6. QC a sample per system: for deletions, re-query for the identifiers; for access, spot-check completeness against the inventory.\n7. Issue the certificate of completion listing systems processed, exceptions applied and the deadline math; emit ask_question immediately if the clock shows fewer than 7 days remaining with work open.\n8. Write dsar-case.toon and log extensions only where the law grants them; the case file is the regulator-facing record.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ncertificate to requester via operator; exception questions to role-general-counsel.\n"
